<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cloud Writer's own launcher glyph, for the Cloud ▸ Tools Primary tile.

  SOURCE: ac_cloud-writer/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_cloud_writer_fg.xml —
  the adaptive-icon FOREGROUND that app ships as its launcher icon. Paths are
  copied verbatim; nothing was redrawn. Copied rather than depended on because
  aa_cloud-superapp does not compile ac_cloud-writer and there is no shared
  icon module — the same reason ic_camera is a copy of Cloud Camera's.

  TWO THINGS CHANGED, both about the box and neither about the art:

  1. VIEWPORT CROPPED 108→56. The source is an adaptive-icon foreground, so
     its art sits inside the 72/108 safe zone with ~26 units of mandated
     margin on every side. Dropped into a 24dp tile that margin is not
     padding, it is a glyph rendered at 46% of the size of every neighbour in
     the row. The group translate re-origins the SAME coordinates onto the
     art's own bounding box (x 28..79, y 34..80 including stroke width), so
     Writer fills its tile exactly as ic_keyboard does.

  2. NO android:tint. ic_keyboard carries tint="?attr/colorOnSurface"; this
     one deliberately does not, and it makes no difference either way —
     TileGridFragment.bindTile and GroupedTilesFragment both overwrite the
     ImageView's imageTintList with the flat palette colour (0xFFE9D8FD) on
     every bind, so ONLY THE SHAPE OF THIS FILE SURVIVES TO THE SCREEN. The
     source's brand colours (#78C8FF accent, #5A7A8C text lines) are kept
     regardless so the file still reads as Writer's icon anywhere it is
     opened, and so a future surface that does not force a tint gets the real
     artwork rather than a silhouette someone has to re-colour.

  When the app IS installed the tile does not use this at all — AppIconTile
  .directIcon pulls the live launcher icon off the device. This is the
  not-installed face of the tile, which is the state it ships in.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="56"
    android:viewportHeight="56">

    <group android:translateX="-26" android:translateY="-30">

        <!-- the written lines, drawn first so the pen sits over them. The last
             one is short and dim: the sentence still being worked on. -->
        <path
            android:strokeColor="#5A7A8C"
            android:strokeWidth="4"
            android:pathData="M30,44 L64,44 M30,56 L58,56" />
        <path
            android:strokeColor="#404040"
            android:strokeWidth="4"
            android:pathData="M30,68 L48,68" />

        <!-- the pen: a nib on a stroke, running up to the right -->
        <path
            android:strokeColor="#78C8FF"
            android:strokeWidth="6"
            android:pathData="M56,72 L76,36" />
        <path
            android:fillColor="#78C8FF"
            android:pathData="M52,80 L57,69 L62,72 Z" />

    </group>
</vector>
